#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Ferry: a mailbox between your devices, over Tailscale. This is a Linux computer's side of it.

    ferry send [FILE…|TEXT]       files, or a text; with nothing: what is piped in, or the clipboard (--to DEVICE: see below)
    ferry list                    what's in the box, numbered: what was received (1 is the newest), then what was sent
    ferry get [N]                 an item (1, the newest received, by default): a text printed, a file copied here
    ferry open | copy N           a file opened, a text to the clipboard
    ferry rm N…                   items out of the box (a received file stays in Downloads)
    ferry clear [received|sent]   everything, or one direction, out of the box
    ferry url | qr                the phone's address (https://<this machine>.<tailnet>.ts.net/ferry/), or Add Device's QR code
    ferry status                  on, or off and why (the server not running)
    ferry enable | disable        the server on/off (ferry.service) and its address on the tailnet
    ferry run                     the server itself (the service)
    ferry app [FILE…]             Ferry's window (files: sends them, after picking the device); --background: the tray
    ferry update [--check]        installs Ferry's newest release (a beta install: the newest pre-release too)
    ferry tray [on|off]           whether the tray icon starts at login (`ferry enable` puts it there)
    ferry version                 this Ferry's version
    ferry list --json             the box and Ferry's state, for a desktop's menu
    ferry qr --svg                the QR code as an SVG file (prints its path), for the menu
    ferry add FILE…               sends files (or a folder's files) without a word (the menu's drop)
    ferry pick                    the same, files chosen in a file dialog (several at once); then the menu says "Sent"
    ferry text TEXT               sends a text
    ferry send-clipboard          sends the clipboard's text (a notification if it has none); to a computer, onto its clipboard
    ferry devices                 the owner's other devices (computers running Ferry, phones that used it), the picked one marked
    ferry target [DEVICE]         the device sends go to (the last one picked), or picks one
    ferry forget DEVICE           a device off every computer's and phone's lists, until it is added again
    ferry seen                    marks what came from the phone as seen (the bar's count goes)
    N is a number from `ferry list`, or an item's id (the menu uses those: numbers change as the box does).
    send, add, pick, text and send-clipboard take --to DEVICE (its name in `ferry devices`) for one send, else the target.

Either end leaves files or text in the box, and they wait there until the other end picks them up. The phone needs no
app: a web page served by this script, which it can add to its Home Screen (a PWA with Web Push notifications). The
devices don't have to be on the same network, only on the same tailnet.

The server listens on localhost only. `tailscale serve` publishes it on the tailnet at MOUNT with the tailnet's real
certificate (iOS writes to the clipboard and allows a PWA and Web Push only on HTTPS), and tells it who is asking: a
request is answered only for the Tailscale user who owns this machine (Tailscale-User-Login, which tailscale serve sets
and a client can't). A custom header on every API call keeps other web pages on the phone from posting here (their
cross-site request would need a CORS preflight, which isn't answered).

Every send goes to one device. For a phone it waits in this computer's box, marked for that phone ("for"): only that
phone's page lists it (the page asks every computer, and each answers with what is for the device asking) and only it
gets the notification. For another computer it goes straight there, as the phone's page sends: it lands in that
computer's box and menu, and Send Clipboard onto its clipboard. The server keeps the owner's computers that answer as
Ferry in STATE/machines.json for the commands and the menu (`ferry devices`).

Several computers: each runs its own Ferry, and the page shows them as one. It asks its own computer which of the owner's
other machines answer at MOUNT (/api/machines), lists what all of them hold, and sends to the one picked above the form,
talking to each directly: a computer answers another one's page (CORS) only if that one belongs to the same owner. A phone's push
subscription belongs to the computer it added the page from, so the others ask that one to pass their notifications on
(/api/relay, /api/relay-push).

A request must name this machine (Host: its tailnet name), so a web page that rebinds its own name to 127.0.0.1 in a
browser here gets nothing. Anyone logged in to this computer could still reach the local port with made-up headers:
Ferry trusts the computer's own users, as a single-user desktop does.

Kept in STATE: items.json (the box), the files left for the phone (files/), the VAPID key for Web Push (made on the first
run; python3-cryptography), the phone's push subscriptions, the phones that have used Ferry here (phones.json: the
device list shows only those) and the devices the owner forgot (forgotten.json, which reaches the other computers
through api/ping). Files from the phone go to Downloads. Items go after
KEEP_DAYS days, a code or a password after SECRET_KEEP or once copied; removing one from the box doesn't delete a file in
Downloads. Nightdrive's Ferry plugin, where this
server came from, kept the same state in OLD_STATE: the first run moves it here (migrate()).

The desktop: the service starts with the user's session, maybe before the desktop, so the desktop's variables (Wayland's
or X11's display) are looked up whenever the clipboard or a notification needs them (desktop_env()). The clipboard is
wl-clipboard's, or xclip's on X11 and where Wayland's can't be reached; notifications go over a session bus connection
of the process's own, through PyGObject, which hears their buttons pressed (Notifications), else they are notify-send's;
how long the computer has been idle comes from the compositor, Mutter, X11 or logind (idle_for()). A desktop's own Ferry
menu hears about changes through HOOK, run with the event's name ("changed": the box or a send; "picked": files sent
from `ferry pick`'s dialog).
"""
import contextlib
import fcntl
import json
import mimetypes
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import threading
import time
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request
from http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer

# The package beside bin/: ~/.local/bin/ferry is a link to bin/ferry, so the real path
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))))
from ferry import config, desktop, forget, idle, notices, push, store, tailnet  # noqa: E402


def probe(host):
    """Ferry on one of the owner's machines: its address, name, tailnet name (id), seconds idle and forgotten devices, or
    None (not running, asleep)."""
    u = f"https://{host}{'' if config.HTTPS_PORT == 443 else f':{config.HTTPS_PORT}'}{config.MOUNT}/"
    try:
        req = urllib.request.Request(u + "api/ping", headers={"X-Ferry": "1"})
        return pinged(host, u, json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=4).read()))
    except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError):
        return None


def pinged(host, u, j):
    """probe()'s answer from a computer's api/ping: with its list of forgotten devices, to merge into this one's."""
    return {"url": u, "name": j.get("computer") or host.split(".")[0], "id": host.split(".")[0], "idle": j.get("idle"),
            "forgotten": j.get("forgotten") if isinstance(j.get("forgotten"), list) else []}


def known_machines(change=None):
    """The owner's computers that answered as Ferry ({id, name, url, idle, seen}), kept by the server for the commands
    and the menu; one that stops answering stays, asleep, while Tailscale still lists it."""
    path = os.path.join(config.STATE, "machines.json")
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            out = json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        out = []
    if change:
        change(out)
        os.makedirs(config.STATE, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
        tmp = path + ".tmp"
        with open(tmp, "w") as f:
            json.dump(out, f, ensure_ascii=False)
        os.replace(tmp, path)
    return out


class Found:
    """The owner's other machines running Ferry, from the ones Tailscale has online. A machine is asked whether it runs
    Ferry when it comes online, again after a minute, and after 10 s if it didn't answer as Ferry (it may have come
    online before its Ferry started). One that goes offline leaves the list at once, and nothing is sent to it: a phone
    asks for this list every 10 s while one of its computers sleeps, instead of trying the sleeping one itself, which
    jammed the phone's Tailscale."""
    AGAIN, MISSED_AGAIN = 60, 10

    def __init__(self, probe=probe, clock=time.monotonic):
        self.probe, self.clock = probe, clock
        self.probed = {}    # host: (when, probe()'s answer or None)
        self.asked = []     # the hosts the last get() asked: only then is there news for known_machines

    def get(self, online):
        now = self.clock()
        due = [h for h in online if h not in self.probed
               or now - self.probed[h][0] > (self.AGAIN if self.probed[h][1] else self.MISSED_AGAIN)]
        self.asked = due
        results = [None] * len(due)

        def one(i, h):
            results[i] = self.probe(h)
        threads = [threading.Thread(target=one, args=(i, h), daemon=True) for i, h in enumerate(due)]
        for t in threads:
            t.start()
        for t in threads:
            t.join(6)
        probed = {h: v for h, v in self.probed.items() if h in online}
        probed.update((h, (now, r)) for h, r in zip(due, results))
        self.probed = probed
        return sorted((r for _, r in probed.values() if r), key=lambda r: r["name"].lower())


STATIC = {"/manifest.webmanifest": "application/manifest+json", "/sw.js": "text/javascript",
          "/icon.svg": "image/svg+xml", "/icon-180.png": "image/png", "/icon-192.png": "image/png",
          "/icon-512.png": "image/png"}


class Ferry:
    def __init__(self):
        self.tailnet = tailnet.Tailnet()
        self.key = push.vapid_key(create=True)
        self.recent = (0.0, None)        # (when, its group): files from the phone in a row, in one notification
        self.lock = threading.Lock()
        self.notifying = threading.Lock()   # one files' notification at a time: each needs the id of the one before
        self.found = Found()             # the owner's other machines running Ferry
        self.used = None                 # phones(), read once: a poll from a phone known already writes nothing
        self.back = False                # whether this computer brought itself back since its Ferry started

    def machines(self):
        """This computer and the owner's other machines that answer as Ferry, as Tailscale has them online now, without
        the forgotten ones. What they forgot is merged into this computer's list (docs/protocol.md › Forgetting a
        device)."""
        self.tailnet.load(force=True)
        found = self.found.get(self.tailnet.machines)
        if self.found.asked:
            now, ids = time.time(), {r["id"] for r in found}

            def merge(known):
                known[:] = [k for k in known if k.get("id") not in ids and k.get("id") in self.tailnet.ids] + \
                           [dict({k: v for k, v in r.items() if k != "forgotten"}, seen=now) for r in found]
            known_machines(merge)
            forget.learn_forgotten([e for r in found for e in r["forgotten"]])
        self.come_back()
        gone = forget.forgotten_ids()
        return [{"url": tailnet.url(), "name": config.alias(), "self": True}] + \
            [{"url": r["url"], "name": r["name"]} for r in found if r["id"] not in gone]

    def come_back(self):
        """This computer's Ferry starting brings it back (docs/protocol.md › What forgetting does): after the first
        round of api/ping, which merged what the others forgot, if its list says it is forgotten. Once per start, so a
        forget heard of later holds until the next one; not before Tailscale names this computer (nobody was asked)."""
        own = self.tailnet.me.split(".")[0].lower()
        with self.lock:
            if self.back or not own:
                return
            self.back = True
        forget.bring_back(own)

    def heard(self, device):
        """A device's call that passed the gate: a phone or a tablet is on the device list from its first one."""
        if device not in self.tailnet.phones:
            return
        if self.used is None:
            self.used = forget.phones()
        if device not in self.used:
            self.used = forget.phones(device)

    # What the phone sends is in the box when the phone is answered; the notification comes after, in a thread of its
    # own, so a notification daemon that is slow or missing doesn't make the phone wait or give up.
    def received_text(self, text, who, clip=False):
        # The phone's Clipboard button means "onto this computer's clipboard": no Copy to press. A typed text waits
        # for one, so it doesn't replace what was just copied here. The phone's clipboard often holds a password from
        # its password manager, so what Send Clipboard puts on this one is marked sensitive, as is a code or a password
        # copied with Copy. A notification doesn't show a code or a password (a desktop may keep what one says), and
        # one leaves the box once copied, so one on the clipboard isn't kept (docs/protocol.md › Codes and passwords).
        it = store.new_item(to="computer", kind="text", text=text, seen=False, **{"from": who})
        hidden = store.looks_secret(text)
        on_clipboard = clip and desktop.copy_text(text, sensitive=True)
        if not (on_clipboard and hidden):
            with store.box(write=True) as items:
                items.append(it)
        if on_clipboard:
            later(notices.notify, f"Copied from {who}", config.SECRET_NAMED if hidden else text[:300])
        else:
            later(notices.notify, f"Text from {who}", config.SECRET_HIDDEN if hidden else text[:300],
                  {"copy": ("Copy", lambda: desktop.copy_text(text, sensitive=hidden) and store.copied(it))})
        desktop.changed()

    def received_file(self, path, size, kind, who, clip=False):
        with store.box(write=True) as items:
            items.append(store.new_item(to="computer", kind="file", name=os.path.basename(path), size=size, type=kind,
                                  path=path, seen=False, **{"from": who}))
        desktop.changed()
        # An image from the phone's clipboard goes onto this one's too, ready to paste; the file stays in Downloads
        if clip and kind.startswith("image/") and desktop.copy_file(path, kind, sensitive=True):
            return later(notices.notify, f"Copied {os.path.basename(path)}",
                         f"From {who} · {os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(path))}", {
                             "open": ("Open", lambda: desktop.open_path(path)),
                             "show": ("Show in Files", lambda: desktop.show_in_files(path))}, desktop.previewable(path, kind))
        with self.lock:
            when, group = self.recent
            if group is None or time.monotonic() - when >= config.GROUP_NOTIFY:
                group = {"paths": [], "nid": "", "shown": 0}   # the files, their notification's id, how many it says
            group["paths"].append(path)
            self.recent = (time.monotonic(), group)
        later(self.notify_files, group, kind, who)

    def notify_files(self, group, kind, who):
        """One notification for files from the phone in a row, each in place of the one before. A folder's files come
        faster than a daemon answers with a notification's id, so they're shown one at a time, each with the files
        that have come by then: one taken with the id it replaces unknown would stay, a stack of "Received N files"."""
        with self.notifying:
            with self.lock:
                paths, old = list(group["paths"]), group["nid"]
            if len(paths) <= group["shown"]:   # the files that came while the one before was shown: said already
                return
            nid = self.files_notification(paths, kind, who, old)
            if old and nid and nid != old:   # a daemon that showed a new one rather than replace it
                notices.close_notification(old)
            with self.lock:
                group["nid"], group["shown"] = nid or old, len(paths)

    def files_notification(self, paths, kind, who, replaces):
        title = f"Received {os.path.basename(paths[-1])}" if len(paths) == 1 else f"Received {len(paths)} files"
        first = paths[0]
        return notices.notify(title, f"From {who} · {os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(paths[-1]))}", {
            "open": ("Open", lambda: desktop.open_path(first if len(paths) == 1 else os.path.dirname(first))),
            "show": ("Show in Files", lambda: desktop.show_in_files(first))},
            desktop.previewable(first, kind) if len(paths) == 1 else "", replaces)


def later(fn, *args):
    threading.Thread(target=fn, args=args, daemon=True).start()


def handler(app):
    class Handler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):
        protocol_version = "HTTP/1.1"
        server_version = "Ferry"

        def log_message(self, fmt, *a):
            """The journal's line for a request, without its query: an upload's carries the file's name
            (docs/protocol.md › api/upload), which isn't the journal's to keep."""
            line = re.sub(r"\?[^\s'\"]*", "", fmt % a)
            print(f"{self.headers.get('X-Forwarded-For', '-') if self.headers else '-'} {line}", flush=True)

        def unread(self):
            """A request body not read yet: answering without it, the connection has to close, or tailscale serve,
            which keeps its connection to us open, would send the next request after the leftover body."""
            if getattr(self, "consumed", False):
                return False
            return int(self.headers.get("Content-Length") or 0) > 0 or \
                "chunked" in (self.headers.get("Transfer-Encoding") or "").lower()

        def send(self, code, body=b"", kind="application/json", headers=None):
            if self.unread():
                self.close_connection = True
                headers = dict(headers or {}, Connection="close")
            if isinstance(body, (dict, list)):
                body = json.dumps(body, ensure_ascii=False).encode()
            elif isinstance(body, str):
                body, kind = body.encode(), "text/plain; charset=utf-8"
            self.send_response(code)
            self.send_header("Content-Type", kind)
            self.send_header("Content-Length", str(len(body)))
            headers = dict({"Cache-Control": "no-cache"}, **(headers or {}))
            origin = self.cors()
            if origin:
                headers.update({"Access-Control-Allow-Origin": origin, "Vary": "Origin"})
            self.send_header("X-Content-Type-Options", "nosniff")
            for k, v in headers.items():
                self.send_header(k, v)
            self.end_headers()
            if self.command != "HEAD":
                self.wfile.write(body)

        def who(self):
            """The asking device's name on the tailnet (tailscale serve gives its address)."""
            ip = (self.headers.get("X-Forwarded-For") or "").split(",")[0].strip()
            return app.tailnet.device(ip) or "your phone"

        def heard(self):
            """The asking device has used Ferry here (docs/protocol.md › Forgetting a device). Only a request through
            tailscale serve names one: a local one with no address would look Tailscale up again every time."""
            if self.headers.get("X-Forwarded-For"):
                app.heard(self.who())

        def cors(self):
            """The asking page's origin if it is another of the owner's machines (its Ferry page switched to this one)."""
            origin = self.headers.get("Origin") or ""
            return origin if origin and app.tailnet.same_owner(origin) else ""

        def gate(self, api):
            """Only the machine's owner, and for the API only a Ferry page: this one, or one on another of the owner's
            machines (see the module's notes)."""
            if not app.tailnet.allowed(self.headers.get("Tailscale-User-Login", "")) or \
                    not app.tailnet.for_me(self.headers.get("Host", "")):
                self.send(403, "Ferry answers only its computer's owner, through Tailscale.")
                return False
            site = self.headers.get("Sec-Fetch-Site", "same-origin")
            if api and (self.headers.get("X-Ferry") != "1" or (site not in ("same-origin", "none") and not self.cors())):
                self.send(403, "Not from the Ferry page")
                return False
            return True

        def do_OPTIONS(self):
            """A CORS preflight from the Ferry page on another of the owner's machines."""
            self.route()
            origin = self.cors()
            if not origin or not app.tailnet.allowed(self.headers.get("Tailscale-User-Login", "")) or \
                    not app.tailnet.for_me(self.headers.get("Host", "")):
                return self.send(403, "Not allowed")
            self.send(204, b"", "text/plain", {"Access-Control-Allow-Methods": "GET, POST",
                                              "Access-Control-Allow-Headers": "X-Ferry, Content-Type",
                                              "Access-Control-Max-Age": "600"})

        def route(self):
            self.consumed = False   # per request: the handler serves every request of a kept-alive connection
            u = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)
            path = u.path
            if path == config.MOUNT or path.startswith(config.MOUNT + "/"):   # in case tailscale serve leaves the mount point on
                path = path[len(config.MOUNT):] or "/"
            return path, dict(urllib.parse.parse_qsl(u.query))

        def read_body(self, limit):
            n = int(self.headers.get("Content-Length") or 0)
            if n > limit:
                raise ValueError("too big")
            self.consumed = True
            return self.rfile.read(n)

        def body(self, limit):
            """The request body in pieces: a Content-Length, or chunked."""
            self.consumed = True   # partly read is unread too: an error ends the connection (upload())
            if "chunked" in (self.headers.get("Transfer-Encoding") or "").lower():
                total = 0
                while True:
                    size = int(self.rfile.readline(1024).split(b";")[0].strip() or b"x", 16)
                    if size == 0:
                        while self.rfile.readline(1024).strip():
                            pass
                        return
                    total += size
                    if total > limit:
                        raise ValueError("too big")
                    while size > 0:
                        chunk = self.rfile.read(min(config.CHUNK, size))
                        if not chunk:
                            raise OSError("connection closed")
                        size -= len(chunk)
                        yield chunk
                    self.rfile.readline(1024)
            else:
                left = int(self.headers.get("Content-Length") or 0)
                while left > 0:
                    chunk = self.rfile.read(min(config.CHUNK, left))
                    if not chunk:
                        raise OSError("connection closed")
                    left -= len(chunk)
                    yield chunk

        def do_HEAD(self):
            self.do_GET()

        def do_GET(self):
            path, q = self.route()
            if not self.gate(api=path.startswith("/api/") and not path.startswith("/api/file/")):
                return
            if path.startswith("/api/"):
                self.heard()
            if path == "/":
                with open(os.path.join(config.WEB, "index.html"), encoding="utf-8") as f:
                    page = f.read().replace("%BASE%", config.MOUNT + "/")
                self.send(200, page.encode(), "text/html; charset=utf-8")
            elif path in STATIC:
                try:
                    with open(os.path.join(config.WEB, path.lstrip("/")), "rb") as f:
                        self.send(200, f.read(), STATIC[path])
                except OSError:
                    self.send(404, "Not found")
            elif path == "/api/items":
                who = self.who()
                with store.box() as items:
                    out = [store.public(i) for i in items if store.for_device(i, who)]
                self.send(200, {"computer": config.alias(), "items": out, "keep": config.KEEP_DAYS, "idle": idle.idle_for(),
                                "push": push.b64u(push.point(app.key)) if app.key else None})
            elif path.startswith("/font/") and path[6:] in config.FONT_FILES:
                try:
                    with open(os.path.join(config.FONTS, path[6:]), "rb") as f:
                        self.send(200, f.read(), "font/ttf", {"Cache-Control": "max-age=604800"})
                except OSError:
                    self.send(404, "Not found")   # the page falls back to the system font
            elif path == "/api/ping":
                self.send(200, {"computer": config.alias(), "idle": idle.idle_for(), "forgotten": forget.forgotten()})
            elif path == "/api/machines":
                self.send(200, {"machines": app.machines(), "push": push.b64u(push.point(app.key)) if app.key else None,
                                "forgotten": forget.forgotten()})
            elif path.startswith("/api/file/"):
                it = store.find(path.rsplit("/", 1)[1])
                if not it or it.get("kind") != "file":
                    return self.send(404, "Not in the box any more")
                self.file(it, q.get("download") == "1")
            else:
                self.send(404, "Not found")

        def file(self, it, attachment):
            try:
                f = open(it["path"], "rb")
            except OSError:
                return self.send(404, "The file is gone")
            with f:
                size = os.fstat(f.fileno()).st_size
                quoted = urllib.parse.quote(it["name"])
                kind = it.get("type") or ""
                inline = bool(config.INLINE.match(kind)) and not attachment
                self.send_response(200)
                self.send_header("Content-Type", kind if config.INLINE.match(kind) else "application/octet-stream")
                self.send_header("Content-Length", str(size))
                self.send_header("Content-Disposition", f"{'inline' if inline else 'attachment'}; filename*=UTF-8''{quoted}")
                self.send_header("X-Content-Type-Options", "nosniff")
                if kind != "application/pdf":   # Safari's PDF viewer doesn't open in a sandbox
                    self.send_header("Content-Security-Policy", "sandbox; default-src 'none'; img-src 'self'; media-src 'self'")
                origin = self.cors()
                if origin:
                    self.send_header("Access-Control-Allow-Origin", origin)
                    self.send_header("Vary", "Origin")
                self.send_header("Cache-Control", "no-cache")
                self.end_headers()
                if self.command == "HEAD":
                    return
                shutil.copyfileobj(f, self.wfile, config.CHUNK)

        def do_POST(self):
            path, q = self.route()
            if not self.gate(api=True):
                return
            self.heard()
            try:
                if path == "/api/text":
                    body = json.loads(self.read_body(config.MAX_TEXT * 2) or b"{}")
                    text = str(body.get("text") or "")
                    if not text.strip():
                        return self.send(400, "Empty text")
                    app.received_text(text[:config.MAX_TEXT], self.who(), clip=bool(body.get("clip")))
                    self.send(200, {"ok": True})
                elif path == "/api/upload":
                    self.upload(q)
                elif path == "/api/clear":
                    # Everything in one direction out of the box (the page's Clear)
                    to = q.get("to", "")
                    with store.box(write=True) as items:
                        for it in [i for i in items if i.get("to") == to]:
                            store.drop_file(it)
                            items.remove(it)
                    desktop.changed()
                    self.send(200, {"ok": True})
                elif path == "/api/remove":
                    store.remove(q.get("id", ""))
                    desktop.changed()
                    self.send(200, {"ok": True})
                elif path == "/api/subscribe":
                    entry = push.subscription(json.loads(self.read_body(8192) or b"{}"), self.who())
                    if not entry:
                        return self.send(400, "Not a push subscription")
                    push.subscribe(entry)
                    self.send(200, {"ok": True})
                elif path in ("/api/forget", "/api/unforget"):
                    # Forgotten on every computer: the others merge this one's list from its api/ping
                    body = json.loads(self.read_body(8192) or b"{}")
                    if path == "/api/unforget" and isinstance(body, dict) and body.get("self") is True:
                        forget.bring_back(self.who())   # a phone just added again with Add Device
                        return self.send(200, {"ok": True})
                    device = body.get("device") if isinstance(body, dict) else None
                    if not forget.device_name(device):
                        return self.send(400, "Not a device's tailnet name")
                    forget.decide(device, path == "/api/forget")
                    self.send(200, {"ok": True})
                elif path == "/api/unsubscribe":
                    end = str(json.loads(self.read_body(8192) or b"{}").get("endpoint", ""))
                    push.subscriptions(lambda s: s.__setitem__(slice(None), [x for x in s if x["endpoint"] != end]))
                    self.send(200, {"ok": True})
                elif path == "/api/relay":
                    # The page from the computer at via, switched to this one: notifications go through via
                    via = str(json.loads(self.read_body(8192) or b"{}").get("via", ""))
                    if not (app.tailnet.same_owner(via) and via.endswith(config.MOUNT + "/")) or via == tailnet.url():
                        return self.send(400, "Not a Ferry page of yours")
                    push.relays(lambda r: r.append(via) if via not in r else None)
                    self.send(200, {"ok": True})
                elif path == "/api/relay-push":
                    # Another of the owner's computers (Tailscale says who asks) notifies this one's phones about itself
                    msg = json.loads(self.read_body(8192) or b"{}")
                    machine = str(msg.get("machine", ""))
                    if not app.tailnet.same_owner(machine):
                        return self.send(400, "Not a Ferry page of yours")
                    push.push_all(str(msg.get("title", ""))[:200], str(msg.get("body", ""))[:300], machine,
                             device=str(msg.get("device", ""))[:100])
                    self.send(200, {"ok": True})
                elif path == "/api/test-push":
                    if not app.key:
                        return self.send(503, "Notifications need python3-cryptography on the computer")
                    push.push_all(config.alias(), "Notifications work")
                    self.send(200, {"ok": True})
                else:
                    self.send(404, "Not found")
            except ValueError:
                self.send(400, "Bad request")

        def upload(self, q):
            n = int(self.headers.get("Content-Length") or 0)
            if n > config.MAX_FILE:
                return self.send(413, f"Too big: {config.human(config.MAX_FILE)} at most")
            dest = config.downloads()
            os.makedirs(dest, exist_ok=True)
            if shutil.disk_usage(dest).free - n < config.MIN_FREE:
                return self.send(507, "Not enough space on the computer")
            while True:   # a name no other upload is writing to at the same time
                path = store.unique(os.path.join(dest, store.safe_name(q.get("name", "file"))))
                part, size = path + ".part", 0
                try:
                    out = open(part, "xb")
                    break
                except FileExistsError:
                    continue
            try:
                with out:
                    for chunk in self.body(config.MAX_FILE):
                        out.write(chunk)
                        size += len(chunk)
            except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
                # Not the path: the file's name stays out of the journal too
                print(f"an upload failed: {e.strerror if isinstance(e, OSError) else e}", flush=True)
                with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
                    os.remove(part)
                self.consumed = False
                return self.send(400, "Upload failed")
            if os.path.exists(path):   # taken meanwhile
                path = store.unique(path)
            os.replace(part, path)
            kind = q.get("type") or mimetypes.guess_type(path)[0] or "application/octet-stream"
            app.received_file(path, size, kind, self.who(), clip=q.get("clip") == "1")
            self.send(200, {"ok": True, "name": os.path.basename(path)})
    return Handler


class Server(ThreadingHTTPServer):
    daemon_threads = True
    allow_reuse_address = True

    def handle_error(self, request, client_address):
        print(f"connection error: {sys.exc_info()[1]!r}", flush=True)   # a phone gone mid-request


def tidy_once():
    """Old items out of the box, also from the disk: a read leaves them in items.json. Written only when one goes."""
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(config.STATE, "items.json")) as f:
            stale = not all(store.alive(i) for i in json.load(f).get("items") or [])
    except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError):
        return False
    if stale:
        with store.box(write=True):
            pass
    return stale


def tidy():
    """Old items out of the box, now and every minute: a code or a password leaves the disk within a minute of its
    SECRET_KEEP (otherwise only a write would notice it)."""
    while True:
        tidy_once()
        time.sleep(60)


def look_around(app):
    """The owner's other computers running Ferry, found again now and then for `ferry devices` (machines.json)."""
    while True:
        try:
            app.machines()
        except Exception as e:   # a thread that dies would leave the list as it was for good
            print(f"looking for the other computers failed: {e!r}", flush=True)
        time.sleep(config.MACHINES_EVERY + 1)   # past Ferry.machines()'s minute, so it looks again


def ask_own(u):
    req = urllib.request.Request(u, headers={"X-Ferry": "1", "User-Agent": f"Ferry/{config.VERSION}"})
    try:
        urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=120).close()
    except urllib.error.HTTPError:
        pass   # an answer all the same: the TLS handshake, which waited for the certificate, is behind it


def warm_certificate(own=None, served=tailnet.serving, get=ask_own):
    """Asks this computer's own https address, so that tailscale serve fetches the tailnet's certificate now: it does
    so on the first request after Ferry is published (36 s for a new machine name), and the phone's first try, right
    after Add Device's QR code is scanned, gives up before that. The address asked, or "" (not published, or no
    answer: try again)."""
    u = (own or tailnet.url)()
    if not u or not served():
        return ""
    try:
        get(u + "api/ping")
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return ""
    return u


def keep_warm():
    """warm_certificate() for each address this computer gets: at start (one quick request when the certificate is
    there already), once it is first published, and when its name changes."""
    warmed = ""
    while True:
        try:
            if tailnet.url() != warmed:
                warmed = warm_certificate()
        except Exception as e:   # a thread that dies would leave a new name's certificate to the phone's first try
            print(f"fetching the certificate failed: {e!r}", flush=True)
        time.sleep(300 if warmed else 20)


def run():
    app = Ferry()
    server = Server(("127.0.0.1", config.PORT), handler(app))
    threading.Thread(target=tidy, daemon=True).start()
    threading.Thread(target=look_around, args=(app,), daemon=True).start()
    threading.Thread(target=idle.WAYLAND_IDLE.run, daemon=True).start()
    threading.Thread(target=keep_warm, daemon=True).start()
    print(f"Ferry on 127.0.0.1:{config.PORT}{'' if app.key else ' (no Web Push: python3-cryptography is missing)'}",
          flush=True)
    server.serve_forever()


def version_key(v):
    """1.0.0-beta.2 sorts before 1.0.0, which sorts before 1.0.1-beta.1."""
    base, _, pre = v.lstrip("v").partition("-")
    nums = tuple(int(n) for n in re.findall(r"\d+", base)[:3])
    return nums + ((0, int((re.findall(r"\d+", pre) or ["0"])[-1])) if pre else (1, 0))


def is_beta(v=None):
    """A beta install is one running a pre-release: it follows pre-releases, until it updates to a full release."""
    return "-" in (config.VERSION if v is None else v)


def newest_release(releases, beta):
    """The newest release with Linux files (GitHub's releases API's list), pre-releases only for a beta:
    {version, tag, tarball, script}, or None."""
    found = []
    for r in releases:
        if r.get("draft") or (r.get("prerelease") and not beta):
            continue
        assets = {a.get("name"): a.get("browser_download_url") for a in r.get("assets") or []}
        if assets.get(config.TARBALL) and assets.get("install.sh"):
            tag = r.get("tag_name", "")
            found.append({"version": tag.lstrip("v"), "tag": tag, "tarball": assets[config.TARBALL],
                          "script": assets["install.sh"]})
    return max(found, key=lambda r: version_key(r["version"]), default=None)


def fetch_releases():
    req = urllib.request.Request(config.RELEASES, headers={"Accept": "application/vnd.github+json",
                                                    "User-Agent": f"Ferry/{config.VERSION}"})
    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=15) as r:
        return json.load(r)


def check_update(fetch=fetch_releases, max_age=None):
    """A release newer than this Ferry, or None; asks GitHub unless it was asked in the last max_age seconds. The
    answer is kept in STATE/update.json for available_update(). A failed check raises (OSError, ValueError)."""
    path = os.path.join(config.STATE, "update.json")
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            cached = json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        cached = {}
    if max_age is None or time.time() - cached.get("checked", 0) > max_age:
        latest = newest_release(fetch(), is_beta())
        cached = {"checked": time.time(), "latest": latest}
        os.makedirs(config.STATE, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
        with open(path + ".tmp", "w") as f:
            json.dump(cached, f)
        os.replace(path + ".tmp", path)
    return available_update(cached)


def available_update(cached=None):
    """The last check's newer release, without asking GitHub."""
    if cached is None:
        try:
            with open(os.path.join(config.STATE, "update.json")) as f:
                cached = json.load(f)
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            return None
    latest = cached.get("latest")
    return latest if latest and version_key(latest["version"]) > version_key(config.VERSION) else None


def update(check_only=False):
    """`ferry update`: the newer release's own install script, run with that release's files, as a first install
    does (the packages it needs, the service restarted)."""
    try:
        new = check_update()
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        print(f"Couldn't check for updates: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    if not new:
        print(f"Ferry {config.VERSION} is the latest" + (" (beta)" if is_beta() else ""))
        return 0
    if check_only:
        print(f"Ferry {new['version']} is out: ferry update installs it")
        return 0
    print(f"Updating Ferry {config.VERSION} to {new['version']}", flush=True)
    tmp = tempfile.mkdtemp()
    try:
        script = os.path.join(tmp, "install.sh")
        req = urllib.request.Request(new["script"], headers={"User-Agent": f"Ferry/{config.VERSION}"})
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=30) as r, open(script, "wb") as f:
            shutil.copyfileobj(r, f)
        env = dict(os.environ, FERRY_DOWNLOAD_URL=new["tarball"])
        return subprocess.run(["bash", script] + (["--beta"] if is_beta(new["version"]) else []), env=env).returncode
    except OSError as e:
        print(f"Couldn't download the update: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(tmp, ignore_errors=True)


def quietly(*cmd):
    with contextlib.suppress(OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        subprocess.run(cmd, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, timeout=30)


def desktop_entry(background=False):
    """Ferry's .desktop file: the window in the app list, and "Open With → Ferry" for any file, which sends it; or
    (background) the tray icon, started at login. It runs this copy of ferry."""
    exe = os.path.join(config.ROOT, "bin", "ferry")
    exe = f'"{exe}"' if re.search(r"[\s\"'\\]", exe) else exe
    lines = ["[Desktop Entry]", "Type=Application", "Name=Ferry", "GenericName=Device Mailbox",
             "Comment=Send texts, the clipboard and files to your other devices over Tailscale",
             f"Icon={config.APP_ID}", "Terminal=false"]
    if background:
        lines += [f"Exec={exe} app --background", "NoDisplay=true", "X-GNOME-Autostart-enabled=true"]
    else:
        lines += [f"Exec={exe} app %F", "Categories=Network;FileTransfer;Utility;",
                  "Keywords=send;share;clipboard;phone;iPhone;Tailscale;",
                  # Open With for any file in KDE, which takes every type as a kind of application/octet-stream. Not
                  # the types themselves: a desktop file in the user's own folder would become their default app
                  # (GNOME's PDFs would open Ferry); the file managers' own menus have "Send with Ferry" instead
                  "MimeType=application/octet-stream;", "StartupNotify=true", "SingleMainWindow=true"]
    return "\n".join(lines) + "\n"


def write_file(path, text):
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)
    with open(path + ".tmp", "w") as f:
        f.write(text)
    os.replace(path + ".tmp", path)


def file_manager_menus():
    """"Send with Ferry" in the file managers' own menus, for the selected files: {path: (text, executable)}. GNOME
    Files has it under Scripts, Dolphin (KDE) and Nemo (Cinnamon) in the menu itself."""
    exe = os.path.join(config.ROOT, "bin", "ferry")
    quoted = f'"{exe}"' if re.search(r"[\s\"'\\]", exe) else exe
    data, home = config.data_home(), os.path.expanduser("~")
    return {
        os.path.join(data, "nautilus", "scripts", "Send with Ferry"):
            (f'#!/bin/sh\n# Ferry\'s "Send with Ferry" in GNOME Files (Scripts): the selected files, after picking the device\n'
             f'exec "{exe}" app "$@"\n', True),
        os.path.join(data, "kio", "servicemenus", config.APP_ID + ".desktop"):
            ("[Desktop Entry]\nType=Service\nMimeType=all/allfiles;\nActions=send;\nX-KDE-Priority=TopLevel\n\n"
             f"[Desktop Action send]\nName=Send with Ferry\nIcon={config.APP_ID}\nExec={quoted} app %F\n", True),
        os.path.join(data, "nemo", "actions", "ferry.nemo_action"):
            ("[Nemo Action]\nName=Send with Ferry\nComment=Send the selected files to one of your devices\n"
             f"Exec={quoted} app %F\nIcon-Name={config.APP_ID}\nSelection=notnone\nExtensions=nodirs;\n", False),
    }


def install_launcher():
    """Ferry in the app list and the file managers' menus, its icon, and its tray icon at login unless
    `ferry tray off`."""
    write_file(os.path.join(config.APPLICATIONS, config.APP_ID + ".desktop"), desktop_entry())
    for path, (text, executable) in file_manager_menus().items():
        write_file(path, text)
        if executable:   # Dolphin runs a service menu only if it is
            os.chmod(path, 0o755)
    for size in (192, 512):
        d = os.path.join(config.ICONS, f"{size}x{size}", "apps")
        os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
        shutil.copyfile(os.path.join(config.WEB, f"icon-{size}.png"), os.path.join(d, config.APP_ID + ".png"))
    set_tray(tray_wanted())
    quietly("update-desktop-database", config.APPLICATIONS)
    quietly("gtk-update-icon-cache", "-q", "-t", config.ICONS)


def tray_wanted():
    return not os.path.exists(config.NO_TRAY)


def set_tray(on):
    """The tray icon at login, or not (remembered across updates)."""
    path = os.path.join(config.AUTOSTART, config.APP_ID + ".desktop")
    if on:
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            os.remove(config.NO_TRAY)
        write_file(path, desktop_entry(background=True))
    else:
        write_file(config.NO_TRAY, "")
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            os.remove(path)


def devices(st=None):
    """The owner's other devices, computers first, without the ones the owner forgot: {id (the short tailnet name),
    name, kind (computer, phone, tablet), online, inUse (a computer in use when last asked)}. Computers are the ones the
    server found running Ferry (machines.json), asleep while Tailscale says they're offline; phones and tablets are
    Tailscale's that have used Ferry here (docs/protocol.md › Forgetting a device)."""
    st = st or tailnet.tailscale_status()
    gone = forget.forgotten_ids()
    me = st.get("Self") or {}
    uid = me.get("UserID")
    peers = {(p.get("DNSName") or "").split(".")[0]: p for p in (st.get("Peer") or {}).values()
             if p.get("UserID") == uid and p.get("DNSName")}
    out = []
    for m in sorted(known_machines(), key=lambda m: m.get("name", "").lower()):
        p = peers.get(m.get("id"))
        if not p or p.get("OS") in ("iOS", "android") or m["id"] in gone:
            continue
        online = bool(p.get("Online"))
        out.append({"id": m["id"], "name": m.get("name") or m["id"], "kind": "computer", "online": online,
                    "inUse": online and m.get("idle") == 0})
    # A phone with a push subscription has used Ferry, also one that did before phones.json was kept (an update)
    used = forget.phones() | {s.get("device") for s in push.subscriptions()}
    for pid, p in sorted(peers.items()):
        if p.get("OS") in ("iOS", "android") and pid in used and pid not in gone:
            tablet = "ipad" in (pid + (p.get("HostName") or "")).lower() or "tablet" in pid.lower()
            out.append({"id": pid, "name": pid, "kind": "tablet" if tablet else "phone", "online": bool(p.get("Online")),
                        "inUse": False})
    return out


def target(devs=None):
    """The device sends go to: the one picked last (STATE/target) while it's still one of the owner's devices, else a
    phone (one online first), else another computer; None when there's no other device."""
    devs = devices() if devs is None else devs
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(config.STATE, "target")) as f:
            picked = f.read().strip()
    except OSError:
        picked = ""
    by_id = {d["id"]: d for d in devs}
    if picked in by_id:
        return by_id[picked]
    phones = [d for d in devs if d["kind"] != "computer"]
    return (sorted(phones, key=lambda d: not d["online"]) or devs or [None])[0]


def set_target(device_id):
    os.makedirs(config.STATE, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    with open(os.path.join(config.STATE, "target"), "w") as f:
        f.write(device_id + "\n")


def mark_sent(what, to, error=""):
    """What was just sent and to whom, for the menu's "Sent" (it shows the newest for a few seconds), or why a send
    didn't go (error), so the menu's button stops waiting."""
    os.makedirs(config.STATE, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = os.path.join(config.STATE, "sent.json.tmp")
    with open(tmp, "w") as f:
        json.dump(dict({"time": time.time(), "what": what, "to": to}, **({"error": error} if error else {})), f,
                  ensure_ascii=False)
    os.replace(tmp, os.path.join(config.STATE, "sent.json"))
    desktop.changed()


def last_sent():
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(config.STATE, "sent.json")) as f:
            d = json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    return d if time.time() - d.get("time", 0) < config.SENT_SHOWN else None


def machine_url(device_id):
    m = next((k for k in known_machines() if k.get("id") == device_id), None)
    return m.get("url", "") if m else ""


def post(u, data, headers):
    req = urllib.request.Request(u, data, method="POST", headers=dict({"X-Ferry": "1"}, **headers))
    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=30) as r:
        return r.read()


def deliver(dev, files=None, text=None, clip=False):
    """Sends files or a text to one device (from devices()): into the box for a phone, straight to another computer.
    clip: it is the clipboard, which another computer puts on its own (a text, or an image file). Returns "" or why it
    failed."""
    if files is not None:
        files = store.file_paths(files)
        if not files:
            return "No files to send there"
        what = os.path.basename(files[0]) if len(files) == 1 else f"{len(files)} files"
    else:
        if not (text or "").strip():
            return "Nothing to send"
        what = oneline(text, 60)
    if dev["kind"] != "computer":
        if files is not None:
            store.add_files(files, dev["id"])
        else:
            store.add_text(text, dev["id"])
    else:
        base = machine_url(dev["id"])
        if not base:
            return f"{dev['name']} isn't running Ferry"
        try:
            if files is None:
                post(base + "api/text", json.dumps({"text": text[:config.MAX_TEXT], "clip": clip}, ensure_ascii=False).encode(),
                     {"Content-Type": "application/json"})
            for path in files or []:
                kind = mimetypes.guess_type(path)[0] or "application/octet-stream"
                q = urllib.parse.urlencode(dict({"name": os.path.basename(path), "type": kind},
                                                **({"clip": "1"} if clip else {})))
                with open(path, "rb") as f:
                    post(base + "api/upload?" + q, f, {"Content-Type": "application/octet-stream",
                                                       "Content-Length": str(os.path.getsize(path))})
        except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
            print(f"send to {base} failed: {e!r}", file=sys.stderr)
            return f"{dev['name']} didn't answer: it's asleep, or Ferry is off there"
    mark_sent(what, dev["name"])
    return ""


def listing():
    st = tailnet.tailscale_status()
    with store.box() as items:
        out = [dict(store.public(i), path=i.get("path", "")) for i in items]
    subs = push.subscriptions() if os.path.exists(os.path.join(config.STATE, "push.json")) else []
    devs = devices(st)
    t = target(devs)
    on = tailnet.systemctl("is-active", "-q", config.SERVICE).returncode == 0
    have = bool(shutil.which("tailscale"))
    served = have and bool(st) and tailnet.serving()
    return {"on": on, "tailscale": st.get("BackendState") == "Running", "url": tailnet.url(st), "serving": served,
            "setup": tailnet.setup_step(st, have, on, served), "push": len(subs), "items": out, "devices": devs,
            "target": t["id"] if t else "", "sent": last_sent(), "version": config.VERSION, "update": available_update()}


def add_link(u):
    """What Add Device's QR code holds for the address `u` (docs/protocol.md › Clients › Adding a phone)."""
    return f"{config.ADD_PAGE}#{u}" if u else ""


def qr(svg):
    u = tailnet.url()
    if not u or not shutil.which("qrencode"):
        print("No address: Tailscale is off" if not u else "qrencode is needed: install it with your package manager",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    if not svg:
        return subprocess.run(["qrencode", "-t", "ANSIUTF8", "-m", "2", add_link(u)]).returncode
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(config.QR), exist_ok=True)
    subprocess.run(["qrencode", "-t", "SVG", "-m", "2", "--foreground=000000", "--background=FFFFFF", "-o", config.QR,
                    add_link(u)], check=True)
    print(config.QR)
    return 0


def ago(t):
    s = time.time() - t
    return "just now" if s < 60 else f"{s // 60:.0f} min ago" if s < 3600 else \
        f"{s // 3600:.0f} h ago" if s < 86400 else f"{s // 86400:.0f} d ago"


def fit(text, room):
    return text if len(text) <= room else text[:room - 1] + "…"


def oneline(text, room):
    return fit(" ".join(text.split()), room)


def print_list():
    items = store.numbered()
    if not items:
        print("The box is empty")
        return
    width, pad, heading = shutil.get_terminal_size().columns, len(str(len(items))), ""
    for n, it in enumerate(items, 1):
        h = "Received" if it.get("to") == "computer" else "Sent, waiting to be picked up"
        if h != heading:
            print(("\n" if heading else "") + h)
            heading = h
        head = f"  {n:>{pad}}  {ago(it.get('time', 0)):<10}  "
        who = f"  · {it['from']}" if it.get("from") else f"  · for {it['for']}" if it.get("for") else ""
        room = max(width - len(head) - len(who), 20)
        what = f"{it.get('name', '')}  {config.human(it.get('size', 0))}" if it.get("kind") == "file" else \
            '"' + oneline(it.get("text", ""), room - 2) + '"'
        print(head + fit(what, room) + who)
    if any(i.get("to") == "computer" and not i.get("seen") for i in items):
        store.mark_seen()
        desktop.changed()


def get(it):
    """A text printed; a file copied to the current folder (its name printed, so `ferry get` works in a script too)."""
    if it.get("kind") == "text":
        text = it.get("text", "")
        sys.stdout.write(text + ("\n" if sys.stdout.isatty() and not text.endswith("\n") else ""))
    else:
        here = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), store.safe_name(it.get("name", "file")))
        if os.path.exists(here) and os.path.samefile(here, it["path"]):   # already here (Downloads)
            dest = here
        else:
            dest = store.unique(here)
            shutil.copy2(it["path"], dest)
        print(os.path.relpath(dest))
    if it.get("to") == "computer" and not it.get("seen"):
        store.mark_seen({it["id"]})
        desktop.changed()
    store.copied(it)   # a code or a password printed is picked up (docs/protocol.md › Codes and passwords)
    return 0


def send(args, dev):
    """Files when every argument is one, a text otherwise; with no arguments, what is piped in or the clipboard."""
    if args in ([], ["-"]):
        piped = args == ["-"] or not sys.stdin.isatty()
        text = sys.stdin.read() if piped else desktop.paste_text()
        if not text.strip():
            print("Nothing to send: " + ("the input is empty" if piped else "the clipboard has no text"), file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        err, what = deliver(dev, text=text), f'"{oneline(text, 60)}"'
    elif any(os.path.exists(p) for p in args):
        missing = [p for p in args if not os.path.exists(p)]
        if missing:
            print(f"No such file: {missing[0]} (to send a text with a file's name, pipe it in)", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        files = store.file_paths(args)
        err = deliver(dev, files=args)
        what = f"{os.path.basename(files[0]) if len(files) == 1 else f'{len(files)} files'}" + \
            (f" ({config.human(sum(os.path.getsize(f) for f in files))})" if files else "")
    else:
        text = " ".join(args)
        err, what = deliver(dev, text=text), f'"{oneline(text, 60)}"'
    if err:
        print(err, file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    print(f"Sent {what} to {dev['name']}", flush=True)
    st = tailnet.status()
    if st != "on" and dev["kind"] != "computer":      # off, or off with why and what turns it on
        print(f"Ferry is {st}, so {dev['name']} can't pick it up yet" + ("" if "(" in st else ": ferry enable"),
              file=sys.stderr)
    return 0


def pick_device(args):
    """--to DEVICE taken out of args: (the device, the rest, ""), or (None, args, why not)."""
    want = ""
    if "--to" in args:
        i = args.index("--to")
        if i + 1 >= len(args):
            return None, args, "--to needs a device: see ferry devices"
        want, args = args[i + 1], args[:i] + args[i + 2:]
    devs = devices()
    dev = next((d for d in devs if want in (d["id"], d["name"])), None) if want else target(devs)
    if not dev:
        return None, args, (f"No device {want}: see ferry devices" if want else
                            "No other device yet: add your phone with Add Device in Ferry's menu (or ferry qr)")
    return dev, args, ""


def failed(err):
    """A send from the menu or a drop that didn't go: nobody sees stderr there."""
    notices.notify("Couldn't send", err)
    mark_sent("", "", err)
    print(err, file=sys.stderr)
    return 1


def pick_files(title):
    """Files chosen in a dialog, several at once: zenity's (GNOME's and most desktops'), else kdialog's (KDE's); None
    without either, [] when none was chosen."""
    home = os.path.expanduser("~/")
    for cmd in (["zenity", "--file-selection", "--multiple", "--separator=\n", f"--title={title}", f"--filename={home}"],
                ["kdialog", "--title", title, "--getopenfilename", home, "--multiple", "--separate-output"]):
        if shutil.which(cmd[0]):
            res = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, env=desktop.desktop_env())
            return [p for p in res.stdout.splitlines() if p]
    return None


def install_unit():
    """The unit into the user's units, its ExecStart naming this copy of ferry (the installed one, or a checkout's)."""
    with open(config.UNIT) as f:
        unit = f.read()
    exe = os.path.realpath(__file__).replace("%", "%%")
    exe = f'"{exe}"' if re.search(r"\s", exe) else exe
    unit = re.sub(r"(?m)^ExecStart=.*$", lambda _: f"ExecStart={exe} run", unit)
    os.makedirs(config.USER_UNITS, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = os.path.join(config.USER_UNITS, config.SERVICE + ".tmp")
    with open(tmp, "w") as f:
        f.write(unit)
    os.replace(tmp, os.path.join(config.USER_UNITS, config.SERVICE))


def enable():
    """The server on: its unit installed and (re)started, so an update runs the new copy, published on the tailnet,
    and the app in the desktop's app list."""
    if not push.vapid_key(create=True):
        print("No python3-cryptography: Ferry works, but without notifications on the phone", file=sys.stderr)
    stop_old()   # its port is this one's
    install_unit()
    install_launcher()
    tailnet.systemctl("daemon-reload")
    for args in (("enable", config.SERVICE), ("restart", config.SERVICE)):
        res = tailnet.systemctl(*args)
        if res.returncode:
            print(res.stderr.strip() or f"systemctl --user {' '.join(args)} failed", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
    if not shutil.which("tailscale"):
        print("Ferry is on, and needs Tailscale to be reached: https://tailscale.com/download/linux, then: ferry enable",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    err = tailnet.serve(True)
    if err:
        print(tailnet.serve_message(err), file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    print(tailnet.url() or "Ferry is on; Tailscale is off, so the page has no address yet")
    return 0


def stop_old():
    """Nightdrive's Ferry plugin's server, off for good: this one takes its port and its state."""
    tailnet.systemctl("disable", "--now", config.OLD_SERVICE)


def migrate(old=config.OLD_STATE, new=config.STATE, stop=stop_old):
    """Moves the state of Nightdrive's Ferry plugin here, once: the VAPID key the phones' subscriptions are bound to,
    the subscriptions, the computers found and the box, so the phones keep their notifications and the box its items.
    True when it moved.

    Under a lock on new's parent folder, so that two commands starting at once neither both move it nor one makes a new
    state (and a new VAPID key) while the other moves the old. The box's paths to files left for the phone are rewritten
    before the move, so no reader ever finds them gone (a write drops items whose file is gone)."""
    if os.path.exists(new) or not os.path.isdir(old):
        return False
    parent = os.path.dirname(new)
    os.makedirs(parent, exist_ok=True)
    fd = os.open(parent, os.O_RDONLY)
    try:
        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        if os.path.exists(new) or not os.path.isdir(old):
            return False
        stop()
        path = os.path.join(old, "items.json")
        try:
            with open(path) as f:
                data = json.load(f)
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            data = None
        if isinstance(data, dict) and isinstance(data.get("items"), list):
            for it in data["items"]:
                p = it.get("path") if isinstance(it, dict) else None
                if isinstance(p, str) and p.startswith(old + os.sep):
                    it["path"] = new + p[len(old):]
            with open(path + ".tmp", "w") as f:
                json.dump(data, f, ensure_ascii=False)
            os.replace(path + ".tmp", path)
        try:
            os.rename(old, new)
        except OSError:   # on another file system
            shutil.copytree(old, new, symlinks=True)
            shutil.rmtree(old)
        os.chmod(new, 0o700)
        return True
    finally:
        os.close(fd)


def main():
    a = sys.argv[1:]
    cmd = a[0] if a else "status"
    try:
        if cmd not in ("version", "--version", "help", "-h", "--help") and migrate():
            print(f"Ferry's state moved from {config.OLD_STATE} to {config.STATE}", file=sys.stderr)
    except OSError as e:   # nothing may start over with a new state (and VAPID key) beside a half-moved one
        print(f"Couldn't move Ferry's state from {config.OLD_STATE} to {config.STATE}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    if cmd == "status":
        print(tailnet.status())
    elif cmd == "enable":
        return enable()
    elif cmd == "disable":
        tailnet.systemctl("disable", "--now", config.SERVICE)
        err = tailnet.serve(False)
        if err:
            print(tailnet.serve_message(err), file=sys.stderr)
    elif cmd == "run":
        run()
    elif cmd == "app":
        sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(config.ROOT, "app"))
        import ferry_app
        return ferry_app.main(sys.modules[__name__], a[1:])
    elif cmd == "update" and a[1:] in ([], ["--check"]):
        return update(check_only=a[1:] == ["--check"])
    elif cmd == "tray" and a[1:] in ([], ["on"], ["off"]):
        if len(a) == 1:
            print("on" if tray_wanted() else "off")
        else:
            set_tray(a[1] == "on")
    elif cmd in ("version", "--version"):
        print(config.VERSION)
    elif cmd == "url":
        u = tailnet.url()
        print(u)
        return 0 if u else 1
    elif cmd == "list" and a[1:] == ["--json"]:
        print(json.dumps(listing(), ensure_ascii=False))
    elif cmd == "list":
        print_list()
    elif cmd in ("send", "add", "pick", "text", "send-clipboard"):
        dev, rest, why = pick_device(a[1:])
        if not dev:
            # A device named with --to that isn't there is that, not "no device yet"
            if cmd == "send":
                print(why, file=sys.stderr)
                return 1
            return failed(why)
        if cmd == "send":
            return send(rest, dev)
        if cmd == "add":
            if not rest:
                return 1
            err = deliver(dev, files=rest)
            return failed(err) if err else 0
        if cmd == "pick":
            paths = pick_files(f"Send to {dev['name']} with Ferry")
            if paths is None:
                return failed("No file dialog here (zenity or kdialog): ferry send FILE sends files")
            if not paths:
                return 1
            err = deliver(dev, files=paths)
            # A menu that closed for the dialog may open again to show what was just sent
            desktop.hook("picked")
            return failed(err) if err else 0
        if cmd == "text":
            if not " ".join(rest).strip():
                return 1
            err = deliver(dev, text=" ".join(rest))
            return failed(err) if err else 0
        text = desktop.paste_text()
        if not text.strip():
            notices.notify("The clipboard has no text", "Copy a text or a link first")
            mark_sent("", "", "The clipboard has no text")
            return 1
        err = deliver(dev, text=text, clip=True)
        return failed(err) if err else 0
    elif cmd == "devices":
        devs = devices()
        t = target(devs)
        for d in devs:
            state = "in use" if d["inUse"] else "online" if d["online"] else \
                "asleep" if d["kind"] == "computer" else "offline"
            print(f"{'*' if t and d['id'] == t['id'] else ' '} {d['id']:<24} {d['kind']:<9} {state}" +
                  (f"  ({d['name']})" if d["name"] != d["id"] else ""))
        if not devs:
            print("No other device yet: add your phone with Add Device in Ferry's menu (or ferry qr)", file=sys.stderr)
    elif cmd == "forget" and len(a) == 2:
        dev = next((d for d in devices() if a[1] in (d["id"], d["name"])), None)
        if not dev:
            print(f"No device {a[1]}: see ferry devices", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        forget.decide(dev["id"], True)
    elif cmd == "target":
        devs = devices()
        if len(a) == 1:
            t = target(devs)
            print(t["id"] if t else "")
            return 0 if t else 1
        dev = next((d for d in devs if a[1] in (d["id"], d["name"])), None)
        if not dev:
            print(f"No device {a[1]}: see ferry devices", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        set_target(dev["id"])
    elif cmd == "get" and len(a) <= 2:
        it = store.item(a[1] if len(a) > 1 else "1")
        if not it or (len(a) == 1 and it.get("to") != "computer"):
            print("Nothing from the phone" if len(a) == 1 else f"No item {a[1]}: see ferry list", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        return get(it)
    elif cmd in ("copy", "open", "rm", "remove") and len(a) > 1:
        items = store.numbered()
        found = [store.item(r, items) for r in a[1:]]   # all first: numbers would change as items go
        if None in found:
            print(f"No item {a[1 + found.index(None)]}: see ferry list", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        for it in found:
            if cmd in ("rm", "remove"):
                store.remove(it["id"])
            elif cmd == "copy" and it.get("kind") == "text":
                if not desktop.copy_text(it["text"], sensitive=store.secret(it)):
                    print("No clipboard to copy to: this needs a desktop", file=sys.stderr)
                    return 1
                store.copied(it)
            elif cmd == "open" and it.get("kind") == "file":
                desktop.open_path(it["path"])
            else:
                print(f"{'Copy' if cmd == 'copy' else 'Open'} is for a {'text' if cmd == 'copy' else 'file'}: "
                      f"ferry get {a[1 + found.index(it)]}", file=sys.stderr)
                return 1
        if cmd in ("rm", "remove"):
            desktop.changed()
    elif cmd == "clear" and len(a) <= 2:
        to = {"": None, "received": "computer", "sent": "phone"}.get(a[1] if len(a) > 1 else "", "?")
        if to == "?":
            print("ferry clear [received|sent]", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        with store.box(write=True) as items:
            for it in [i for i in items if to is None or i.get("to") == to]:
                store.drop_file(it)
                items.remove(it)
        desktop.changed()
    elif cmd == "seen":
        store.mark_seen()
    elif cmd == "qr":
        return qr(a[1:] == ["--svg"])
    elif cmd in ("help", "-h", "--help"):
        print(__doc__.split("\n\n")[1])
    else:
        print(__doc__.split("\n\n")[1], file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    return 0

if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
